providers/default-service-beside-a-named-one.toml is not a valid connector definition:
  - `[[services]]` declares "default" beside the named service "chat". "default" may be declared only by a provider whose *only* API surface it is, and only to carry `roles` — which a single-surface provider has nowhere else to put. A provider that declares named services has no implicit "default" for an operation to fall into, and declaring one here would hand it back: an operation that omitted `service` would become legal and be emitted into a `<provider>-default.flux` nobody asked for. Declare the roles on the service that actually has them
